Ok, good.

As far as your follow-up question, the mcmc should be estimating `lambda` already, but nimble only returns samples for the top-level parameters by default. Please see this manual section <https://r-nimble.org/html_manual/cha-mcmc.html#monitors-and-thinning-intervals-printmonitors-getmonitors-setmonitors-addmonitors-resetmonitors-and-setthin> on setting monitors.

-chris

